g referring to two separate diseases (breast cancer and ovarian cancer), so it is one Composite Mention.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate 2: Annotate contiguous text strings (Composite Mention)\"},{\"id\":4,\"entity\":\"NONE\",\"rationale\":\"'malignant effusions' only names the specimen source (fluid samples) and describes a general finding or complication rather than a named specific or class disease, so it is not annotated.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What NOT to Annotate 4: Do not annotate general terms (e.g., complications, abnormalities)\"},{\"id\":5,\"entity\":\"Modifier\",\"rationale\":\"'breast cancer' in 'many breast cancer biopsies' is a disease name modifying the noun 'biopsies', so it is annotated as a Modifier.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate 3: Annotate disease mentions that are used as Modifiers for other concepts\"},{\"id\":6,\"entity\":\"DiseaseClass\",\"rationale\":\"'breast cancers' is the head noun referring to a family of multiple diseases, explicitly divided into sporadic and familial forms, so it is a Disease Class mention.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate 1: Disease Class (mentions describing a family of multiple specific diseases)\"},{\"id\":7,\"entity\":\"NONE\",\"rationale\":\"'sporadic' is an adjective describing the type of cancer, not a disease name, so it is not a disease mention.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What NOT to Annotate 4: Do not annotate general terms; only disease name mentions are annotated\"},{\"id\":8,\"entity\":\"NONE\",\"rationale\":\"'familial' is an adjective describing the form of cancer, not a disease name, so it is not a disease mention.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What NOT to Annotate 4: Do not annotate general terms; only disease name mentions are annotated\"}]}", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_inpu